<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Soviet Union</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Soviet</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Soviet Union was a communist state that existed from 1922 to 1991, established on the territory of the former <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russian-empire">Russian Empire</a> after the revolutions of 1917. It became a superpower after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a>. Accounts of the Russian Empire treat it as the successor to the tsarist empire, and accounts of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/empire-of-japan">Empire of Japan</a> note its role in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a>'s defeat.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/soviet-union.jpg" alt="Soviet Union" width="320" height="160" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: СССР · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Soviet_Union.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
